WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.720
The first season of The Mandalorian, which
launched with the Disney+ streaming platform

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.600
in 2019, has proven a huge success with both
critics and audiences.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.800
As its eight episodes rolled out, the Star
Wars franchise seemed to achieve something

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.520
it hasn't had in years: a unified fanbase.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.220
Being near-universally beloved is not something
that comes easily for Star Wars anymore.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.740
The Force Awakens was a crowd-pleaser, but
faced criticism for its adherence to the classic

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.940
Star Wars formula.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.420
The Last Jedi proved bitterly divisive among
fans who either loved or hated it.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.380
And then there's The Rise of Skywalker…

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.200
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.030
Rise of Skywalker instantly took the dubious
distinction of being the worst-reviewed of

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.040
all the live-action Star Wars movies.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.340
On top of all that, there are still the ongoing
debates as to the merits of the prequel trilogy

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.200
and the expanded universe canon.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.879
All of this is to say that The Mandalorian's
success is important for the franchise's good

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.200
name, and for the fans.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.260
And that means those fans want more Mandalorian
and they want it ASAP.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.900
Unfortunately, one new adventure for our lone
hunter and cub just got delayed.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:08.060
In June 2020, Disney and Lucasfilm revealed
a full line-up of Mandalorian-related books

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:12.859
designed to sate the appetite of fans eagerly
awaiting season 2, which is set to arrive

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.500
in October 2020.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.080
Among the promised titles are in-depth tie-ins
like The Art of The Mandalorian and The Ultimate

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:24.229
Visual Guide, a junior novelization for young
adults, a pair of kids' storybooks, and an

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:27.100
as-yet untitled Mandalorian original novel.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.299
Many of these might seem insignificant to
the average adult reader, but we're talking

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.500
about Star Wars here.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:38.119
Every Star Wars background player and location
inevitably gets its own action figure or playset

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.480
because fans are obsessed about understanding
every square millimeter of the universe.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.520
Even a junior novelization might hold some
teeny detail for fans to salivate over and

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.560
speculate about.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.110
Obviously, though, the two big titles there
are The Art of The Mandalorian and that untitled

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:56.760
original novel, both set for a December 2020
release.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.759
As of now, the art book is still on schedule,
but on August 3, 2020, Del Rey Publishing

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.720
tweeted that The Mandalorian novel's release
date has been moved back to the fall of 2021.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.320
There isn't a lot known about the original
Mandalorian novel so far.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.220
Its author, Adam Christopher, has written
books for several other pop culture licenses,

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:18.420
including Stranger Things, Dishonored, and
Elementary.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.760
Christopher has also written for Star Wars
before, as one of the authors of Star Wars:

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.180
"From a certain point of view."

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.480
"A certain point of view?"

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.620
Yes, Luke, Star Wars: From a Certain Point
of View - a short story anthology retelling

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.959
the events of the original Star Wars movie
from the perspectives of various supporting

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:36.720
characters.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.020
As to exactly why the book is delayed, unfortunately,
we don't have an explanation.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.040
While many might jump to the conclusion that
the release was stymied by the ongoing pandemic,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.480
there's been no indication that that's the
case.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.940
Christopher's comments regarding the alteration
were simple, as he tweeted:

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.740
"Fear not, fellow Covert members!

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.840
THE MANDALORIAN will hit the shelves next
year, and you will *not* be disappointed."

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.220
Fortunately, there are other Star Wars books
still coming out between now and fall 2021.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.220
In addition to The Mandalorian art book, there's
Alex Segura's Poe Dameron: Free Fall, released

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.420
on August 4.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:13.340
Segura's book focuses on a teenage Poe, the
strained relationship he has with his father,

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:16.940
and the early adventures that lead to his
relationship with Zorii Bliss.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.280
Popular Star Wars novelist Timothy Zahn is
returning to the character who made him such

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:27.150
a popular author with Star Wars: Thrawn Ascendancy:
Chaos Rising, Book 1, slated to arrive on

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.980
September 1, 2020.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.680
The new novel, much like Segura's Poe Dameron
adventure, is set in the past, long before

00:03:33.689 --> 00:03:35.340
Thrawn became a famed general.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.160
The story follows his first command.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:42.120
And, of course, early 2021 will see the release
of Star Wars: The High Republic, a major new

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:47.040
initiative that will span both across books
and comics featuring stories set some 200

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.260
years before the Skywalker Saga.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.519
Basically, there's plenty to chew on in the
land of Star Wars books.

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:57.280
And furthermore, The Mandalorian's second
season is just a scant few months away, set

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.400
to stream on Disney+ in October 2020.

